1
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:38,909
Wet soil and eucalyptus leaves,

2
00:00:42,200 --> 00:00:47,299
Anemones in a zinc bucket.

3
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:54,880
Quiet Thursday in the shop,

4
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:02,500
Where no one asks me to be a puppet.

5
00:01:07,200 --> 00:01:12,400
Two minutes in the green,

6
00:01:15,659 --> 00:01:22,180
A lion in a blue wool sweater.

7
00:01:23,200 --> 00:01:28,900
Between the roses and the shade,

8
00:01:31,500 --> 00:01:38,340
I’ll hold you close forever.

9
00:01:47,200 --> 00:01:52,670
An old man buys his yellow blooms,

10
00:01:55,500 --> 00:02:00,390
My hands are shaking at the seam.

11
00:02:03,319 --> 00:02:08,050
Then suddenly you’re standing there,

12
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,110
A boy dancing through my dreams.

13
00:02:20,039 --> 00:02:26,680
Two minutes freezing time,

14
00:02:28,099 --> 00:02:34,819
Your arm turns solid under wool.

15
00:02:35,900 --> 00:02:42,310
A king who stumbles in the shop,

16
00:02:43,849 --> 00:02:52,300
And makes my guarded heart feel full.

17
00:02:52,379 --> 00:02:57,409
You blush and stare at your shoes,

18
00:03:00,199 --> 00:03:07,189
With books in your bag.

19
00:03:07,280 --> 00:03:13,300
Shy behind your gentle eyes,

20
00:03:14,169 --> 00:03:22,610
Raising up my red-satin flag.

21
00:03:23,430 --> 00:03:30,680
Two minutes in the dark,

22
00:03:30,930 --> 00:03:37,919
Sunday night will bring the fire.

23
00:03:37,960 --> 00:03:45,900
On the parket I’ll ask my question,

24
00:03:46,680 --> 00:03:51,180
Drowning us both in raw desire.

25
00:03:54,969 --> 00:03:58,969
Back to school, my engineer.

26
00:04:02,990 --> 00:04:07,289
Trim the lilies, wipe the shelf.

27
00:04:10,319 --> 00:04:15,449
Two minutes changed my world today,

28
00:04:18,779 --> 00:04:22,779
I’ll never let you hide yourself.